# One asynchronous language connection can analyze independent editor projects.
# Work is protocol data. A platform supplies transport, never editor policy.
import source_protocol.dl

the UI source analysis delay means: 0.18

to get [UI language work] {a pointer to JSON value:payload} [at step] {integer:step} [in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    set client's phase to step
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI language work, step, payload)

to get [UI language message] {string:method} [with] {a pointer to JSON value:parameters} [requesting] {boolean:request} [at step] {integer:step} [in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    set message to a JSON object containing [JSON text "jsonrpc" is "2.0", JSON text "method" is method, JSON child "params" is parameters]
    if request:
        add a JSON member named "id" with value (a new JSON-RPC integer for step) to message
    return UI language work (a JSON object containing [JSON text "operation" is "exchange", JSON child "message" is message]) at step step in client

to get [the UI language project at step] {integer:step} [in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    set project to client's desired's project
    set document to project's entry
    forget UI language models in client
    set client's project to project
    set client's model to the UI language model for document in client
    set client's uri to document's uri
    set client's context to document's context
    set client's project context to document's project's context
    set client's profiles to the compact JSON form of (document's project's profiles)
    set files to the UI source files of project
    return UI language work (a JSON object containing [JSON text "operation" is "project", JSON child "sources" is files]) at step step in client

to get [the UI language opening in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    set document to client's document
    set client's uri to document's uri
    set client's context to document's context
    set client's opened to true
    set client's snapshot to document's prefix + document's source
    set client's revision to document's revision
    set client's project revision to document's project's revision
    set client's version to 1
    if document = document's project's entry:
        begin UI source reports for (document's project)
    set parameters to the LSP document opening parameters for URI (client's uri), language (the string form of "dynlex"), version 1 and text (client's snapshot)
    return UI language message "textDocument/didOpen" with parameters requesting false at step 4 in client

to get [the UI language token request in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    set client's project revision to client's document's project's revision
    set client's token epoch to client's document's token epoch
    set parameters to a JSON object containing [JSON child "textDocument" is (an LSP text document identifier for (client's uri))]
    return UI language message "textDocument/semanticTokens/full" with parameters requesting true at step 6 in client

to get [the UI language source change in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    set document to client's document
    set client's snapshot to document's prefix + document's source
    set client's revision to document's revision
    set client's project revision to document's project's revision
    increment client's version
    begin UI source reports for (document's project)
    set parameters to the LSP document change parameters for (client's uri) at (client's version) containing (a full LSP content change containing (client's snapshot))
    return UI language message "textDocument/didChange" with parameters requesting false at step 5 in client

to get [the next UI language project closing in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    set model to client's models
    loop while model != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI language document):
        if model's opened:
            set client's model to model
            set model's opened to false
            return UI language message "textDocument/didClose" with (the LSP document closing parameters for URI (model's uri)) requesting false at step 9 in client
        set model to model's next
    return the UI language project at step 10 in client

to get {a pointer to UI language document:model} [has current UI model text]:
    set document to model's document
    return (model's revision = document's revision) and (model's context = document's context)

to get [the next UI language work for] {a pointer to UI language client:client} [analyzing] {a pointer to UI source document:document} [at] {floating-point number:seconds} [seconds]:
    set client's desired to document
    if (client's phase != 0) and (client's phase != 7):
        return a new UI language work
    set query to the next pending UI source query in document
    set pending to query != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI source query)
    set main to document's project's entry
    if (((document needs UI source analysis) = false) and ((main needs UI source analysis) = false)) and (pending = false):
        return a new UI language work
    if (pending = false) and ((document's analyzed revision != document's revision) and (seconds < (document's edited at + (the UI source analysis delay)))):
        return a new UI language work
    if client's phase = 0:
        return the UI language project at step 1 in client
    if client's profiles != (the compact JSON form of (document's project's profiles)):
        mark UI language models closed in client
        return UI language work (a JSON object containing [JSON text "operation" is "reset"]) at step 11 in client
    if (client's project != document's project) or (client's project context != document's project's context):
        return the next UI language project closing in client
    set root to the UI language model for main in client
    set client's model to root
    if root's opened = false:
        return the UI language opening in client
    if (root has current UI model text) = false:
        return the UI language source change in client
    if main needs UI source analysis:
        return the UI language token request in client
    if document's available = false:
        return a new UI language work
    set model to the UI language model for document in client
    set client's model to model
    if model's opened = false:
        return the UI language opening in client
    if (model has current UI model text) = false:
        return the UI language source change in client
    if document needs UI source analysis:
        return the UI language token request in client
    require condition pending reporting "An editor feature has no pending request"
    set client's query to query
    set client's query generation to query's generation
    set client's query notification to query's notification
    set query's queued to false
    return UI language message (query's method) with (a copy of JSON-RPC node (query's parameters)) requesting (query's notification = false) at step 12 in client

to get {a pointer to UI language client:client} [has current UI language source]:
    set document to client's document
    return ((client's opened) and ((document's revision = client's revision) and (document's context = client's context))) and ((client's project context = document's project's context) and (client's project revision = document's project's revision))

to [receive UI language diagnostics] {a pointer to JSON value:response} [in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    if (client has current UI language source) = false:
        return nothing
    set index to 0
    loop while index < response's length:
        set message to the JSON value at index index in response
        if message has JSON member named "method":
            if (the JSON text named "method" in message) = "textDocument/publishDiagnostics":
                set parameters to the JSON member named "params" in message
                retain UI source diagnostics (the JSON member named "diagnostics" in parameters) at (the JSON text named "uri" in parameters) in (client's project)
        increment index

to get [advance UI language reply] {a pointer to JSON value:response} [at step] {integer:step} [in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    if step = 1:
        set capabilities to the default LSP client capabilities
        parse (client's profiles) as JSON and set parsed to it
        set options to a JSON object containing [JSON child "dynlex" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "analysisProfiles" is (the value of parsed)])]
        set parameters to the LSP initialization parameters rooted at (client's root) with capabilities and initialization options options
        free capabilities
        free options
        return UI language message "initialize" with parameters requesting true at step 2 in client
    if step = 2:
        set result to the UI language result numbered 2 in response
        set provider to the JSON member named "semanticTokensProvider" in (the JSON member named "capabilities" in result)
        free client's token types
        set client's token types to a copy of JSON-RPC node (the JSON member named "tokenTypes" in (the JSON member named "legend" in provider))
        return UI language message "initialized" with (a new JSON-RPC object) requesting false at step 3 in client
    if (step = 3) or (step = 10):
        return the UI language opening in client
    if (step = 4) or (step = 5):
        return the UI language token request in client
    if step = 6:
        set tokens to the UI language result numbered 6 in response
        if client has current UI language source:
            set document to client's document
            if (UI semantic tokens tokens using (client's token types) match UI source document document) = false:
                increment document's token generation
            free document's tokens
            free document's token types
            set document's tokens to a copy of JSON-RPC node tokens
            set document's token types to a copy of JSON-RPC node (client's token types)
            set document's token revision to client's revision
            set document's analyzed token epoch to client's token epoch
            set document's analyzed revision to client's revision
            set document's analyzed project revision to client's project revision
            if document = document's project's entry:
                finish UI source reports for (document's project)
        set client's phase to 7
        return a new UI language work
    if step = 9:
        if client's profiles != (the compact JSON form of (client's desired's project's profiles)):
            mark UI language models closed in client
            return UI language work (a JSON object containing [JSON text "operation" is "reset"]) at step 11 in client
        return the next UI language project closing in client
    if step = 11:
        return the UI language project at step 1 in client
    if step = 12:
        set query to client's query
        set result to a new JSON-RPC null
        if client's query notification = false:
            free result
            set result to a copy of JSON-RPC node (the UI language result numbered 12 in response)
        if (client has current UI language source) and (query's generation = client's query generation):
            if query is current for UI source document (client's document):
                free query's result
                set query's result to result
                set query's ready to true
                set result to a new JSON-RPC null
        free result
        set client's query to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI source query)
        set client's phase to 7
        return a new UI language work
    require condition false reporting "An unknown language-service step completed"
    return a new UI language work

to get [the next UI language server reply in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    if client's reply index < client's replies' length:
        set message to a copy of JSON-RPC node (the JSON value at index (client's reply index) in (client's replies))
        increment client's reply index
        return UI language work (a JSON object containing [JSON text "operation" is "exchange", JSON child "message" is message]) at step 13 in client
    free client's replies
    set client's replies to a new JSON-RPC array
    set client's reply index to 0
    set work to client's continuation
    set client's continuation to a new UI language work
    set client's phase to client's continuation phase
    return work

to get [the UI language reply] {a pointer to JSON value:response} [at step] {integer:step} [in] {a pointer to UI language client:client}:
    require condition (client's phase = step) reporting "A language-service reply arrived out of order"
    receive UI language server messages response in client
    receive UI language diagnostics response in client
    if step = 13:
        return the next UI language server reply in client
    set work to advance UI language reply response at step step in client
    if client's reply index < client's replies' length:
        set client's continuation to work
        set client's continuation phase to client's phase
        return the next UI language server reply in client
    return work
